        "objective": "Distinguish and accurately apply the fundamental differences between 'Por' (motion through space, contractions pela/pelo, duration, means, cause) and 'Para' (destination, recipient, deadline, purpose) in Brazilian Portuguese travel contexts.",
        "presentation": {
            "explanation": "The **POR vs. PARA** distinction in Brazilian Portuguese governs all travel, navigation, and itinerary phrasing:\n\n1. When to use **POR** (Contractions: **pelo = por+o**, **pela = por+a**, **pelos**, **pelas**):\n   - **Motion Through / Along Space**: *Caminhar **pela** Avenida Paulista / Passear **pelo** calçadão de Copacabana.* (Walking along/through the avenue/boardwalk).\n   - **Means of Communication or Transit**: *Mandar a localização **por** WhatsApp / Viajar **por** trem.* (Via WhatsApp, by train).\n   - **Duration of Time**: *Fiquei no Rio **por** cinco dias.* (For 5 days).\n   - **Cause / Reason ('Because of / Due to')**: *O voo atrasou **por** causa da chuva.* (Due to rain).\n\n2. When to use **PARA** (often contracted to **pra / pro** in spoken Brazilian Portuguese):\n   - **Physical Destination**: *Esse ônibus vai **para** Ipanema / Vamos **pro** aeroporto.* (Heading to Ipanema / airport).\n   - **Purpose / Goal ('In order to' + Infinitive)**: *Comprei o Bilhete Único **para** andar de metrô.* (In order to ride).\n   - **Deadline / Specific Future Time**: *O relatório é **para** amanhã / O voo é **para** as oito.* (For tomorrow / 8:00).\n   - **Recipient**: *Esse presente é **para** você.* (For you).\n\n3. The Spatial Contrast Test:\n   - *Passamos **pelo** túnel* (We pass **through** the tunnel — path).\n   - *Vamos **para** o museu* (We go **towards / to** the museum — destination).",
            "examples": [
                {
                    "target": "Caminhamos pela praia de Copacabana para ver o pôr do sol no Arpoador.",
                    "reading": "Caminhamos pela praia de Copacabana para ver o pôr do sol no Arpoador.",
                    "translation": "We walk along Copacabana beach in order to see the sunset at Arpoador."
                },
                {
                    "target": "Esse ônibus vai para a Barra da Tijuca e passa pela Zona Sul.",
                    "reading": "Esse ônibus vai para a Barra da Tijuca e passa pela Zona Sul.",
                    "translation": "This bus goes towards Barra da Tijuca and passes through the South Zone."
                },
                {
                    "target": "O metrô parou por causa de uma queda de energia.",
                    "reading": "O metrô parou por causa de uma queda de energia.",
                    "translation": "The subway stopped because of a power outage."
                }
            ],
            "mnemonics": [
                "POR (pelo/pela) = Path through space, Means, Duration, Cause (The Journey)!",
                "PARA (pra/pro) = Destination, Purpose (In order to), Deadline, Recipient (The Goal)!",
                "Vai PRA (destination) / Passa POR (route)!"
            ],
            "culturalNotes": [
                "Watching the sunset at Pedra do Arpoador between Copacabana and Ipanema is a sacred Rio de Janeiro ritual, where crowds traditionally applaud when the sun sinks into the Atlantic Ocean."
            ]
        },
