        "presentation": {
            "explanation": "Nelson Rodrigues (1912–1980 - Recife & Rio de Janeiro) and the birth of modern Brazilian dramaturgy:\n- **Nelson Rodrigues (\"O Anjo Pornográfico\" / The Pornographic Angel)**:\n  - The undisputed father of modern Brazilian theater; journalist, chronicler, and tragic dramatist;\n- The Historic Masterpiece: **«Vestido de Noiva» (The Wedding Dress - Premiered December 28, 1943 at the Theatro Municipal do Rio de Janeiro)**:\n  - Directed by Polish exile **Zbigniew Ziembinski** with the company *Os Comediantes*;\n  - Single-handedly ended the era of shallow French boulevard comedies, launching modern psychological expressionism in Brazil;\n  - **The 3 Simultaneous Planes of Consciousness**:\n    - 1. **O Plano da Realidade (The Plane of Reality)**: Madame Clessi's brothel / the operating room where protagonist Alaíde lies dying after a car crash;\n    - 2. **O Plano da Memória (The Plane of Memory)**: Alaíde recalling how she stole her fiancé Pedro from her sister Lúcia;\n    - 3. **O Plano da Alucinação (The Plane of Hallucination)**: Surreal fever dreams where Alaíde converses with murdered 1905 prostitute Madame Clessi in a bloodstained wedding gown;\n  - Unsparing psychological dissection of bourgeois hypocrisy, incestuous desires, jealousy, and guilt.",
            "examples": [
                {
                    "target": "A estreia de «Vestido de Noiva» de Nelson Rodrigues em 1943, dirigida por Ziembinski, fundou o teatro moderno brasileiro ao dividir o palco em Realidade, Memória e Alucinação.",
                    "reading": "A es-trey-a de Ves-tee-do de Noy-va...",
                    "translation": "The 1943 premiere of Nelson Rodrigues' \"The Wedding Dress,\" directed by Ziembinski, founded modern Brazilian theater by dividing the stage into Reality, Memory, and Hallucination."
                }
            ],
            "mnemonics": [
                "Nelson Rodrigues (Father of Modern Brazilian Theater & Anjo Pornográfico)! Vestido de Noiva 1943 (Ziembinski direction)! 3 Planes: Realidade, Memória, Alucinação! Álbum de Família!"
            ],
            "culturalNotes": [
                "The Brazilian federal censorship under the Getúlio Vargas Estado Novo regime was so scandalized by Nelson Rodrigues' *Álbum de Família* that the play was completely banned from the stage for 21 years until 1965."
            ]
        },
