            "explanation": "Augusto Boal (1931–2009 - Rio de Janeiro & São Paulo/Paris) and the worldwide revolution of the Theatre of the Oppressed:\n- **Augusto Boal**:\n  - Playwright, director, and theorist; artistic director of the **Teatro de Arena de São Paulo** alongside Gianfrancesco Guarnieri (*Eles Não Usam Black-tie*); nominated for the **Nobel Peace Prize**.\n- The Theoretical Masterpiece: **«Teatro do Oprimido» (Theatre of the Oppressed - 1971–1974)**:\n  - Developed while imprisoned, tortured, and exiled by the Brazilian military dictatorship;\n  - Influenced by Paulo Freire's *Pedagogy of the Oppressed*;\n  - **The \"Spect-Actor\" (O Espect-Ator)**: Abolished the passive boundary between actor and audience; transformed spectators into active protagonists who step onto the stage to rehearse real social change;\n- The Core Methodologies:\n  - **Forum Theatre (Teatro Fórum)**: A scene of social oppression is performed; the *Kuringa* (Joker/Facilitator) stops the play and invites audience members to shout \"STOP!\", take the actor's place on stage, and physically improvise alternative solutions to overcome the oppression;\n  - **Invisible Theatre (Teatro Invisível)** & **Legislative Theatre (Teatro Legislativo)**: Using theatrical forums to write actual municipal laws in Rio de Janeiro.",
