            "explanation": "Eduardo Viveiros de Castro (1951–present - Rio de Janeiro) and the ontological revolution of Amerindian Perspectivism:\n- **Eduardo Batalha Viveiros de Castro**:\n  - Brazilian anthropologist and philosopher; Professor of Social Anthropology at the Museu Nacional (UFRJ); Doctor Honoris Causa from Paris Nanterre; recognized globally as the leader of the **\"Ontological Turn\" in world philosophy and anthropology**.\n- The Revolutionary Metaphysical Breakthrough: **Amerindian Perspectivism (Perspectivismo Ameríndio)**:\n  - **Western Naturalism vs Amazonian Multinaturalism**:\n    - **Western Multiculturalism**: Believes in **One Nature** (fixed objective physical universe governed by physics) and **Many Cultures** (human subjective interpretations);\n    - **Amerindian Multinaturalism (Multinaturalismo)**: Inverts the Western paradigm: **One Culture (Universality of Spirit)** and **Many Natures (Multiplicity of Bodies)**;\n    - Indigenous Amazonian cosmology posits that all beings (jaguars, tapirs, trees, spirits) possess the same human soul/subjectivity; what differs is their **bodily clothing/envelope** (*vestimenta corporal*);\n    - To a jaguar, it sees itself as a human being, it drinks blood as manioc beer, and it sees human beings as prey animals;\n  - **«Metafísicas Canibais» (Cannibal Metaphysics - 2009)**: Proposes \"decolonizing thought\" by treating indigenous Amazonian metaphysics not as primitive folklore, but as a sophisticated philosophical system that challenges Western anthropocentrism.",
