            "explanation": "Cozinha Mineira and the comforting rural culinary sanctuary of Minas Gerais:\n- **The Terroir of Minas Gerais (A Cozinha da Roça)**:\n  - Born in the 18th-century gold and diamond mining boom (*Ciclo do Ouro*);\n  - Rooted in slow cooking over traditional wood-burning clay stoves (**fogão a lenha**), heavy soapstone pots (**panela de pedra-sabão**), and copper cauldrons;\n- Master Artisanal Treasures:\n  - **Queijo Minas Artesanal da Serra da Canastra (IPHAN Heritage & World Cheese Awards Champion)**:\n    - Made from fresh raw cow's milk (*leite cru*) inoculated with endogenous whey ferment (**pingo**), pressed by hand, and cured for 21 to 60 days on wooden boards in the microclimate of the Canastra mountains;\n  - **The Perfect Pão de Queijo (Cheese Bread)**:\n    - Made with fermented sour manioc starch (**polvilho azedo**), eggs, lard/butter, and cured Queijo Canastra (never wheat flour or yeast!);\n    - Produces a golden crust with an elastic, chewy, airy, cheese-stretching crumb;\n  - **Feijão Tropeiro**:\n    - Created by 18th-century muleteers (*tropeiros*) transporting gold through the wilderness: brown beans mixed with manioc flour, diced fried bacon, linguiça, scrambled eggs, and fresh collard greens;\n  - **Frango com Quiabo** (braised free-range chicken with non-slimy charred okra) & **Doce de Leite Mineiro** stirred for hours in copper cauldrons with pure sugar.",
